he Catholic Church", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T16:25:47Z", "username": "Dr.Namrata Srinivasan", "text": "Diet of worms could be a quiz question by itself🤣", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T16:26:09Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "For the next question, I will accept either of two answers", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T16:26:13Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "10.\tGeorge Fox founded a religious movement during the turbulent English Civil War period. In 1647, he reported a spiritual experience on Pendle Hill in Lancashire that inspired him to preach. He taught that every person has direct access to God through an “Inner Light” and rejected formal clergy, creeds, and the sacraments. His followers were originally called “Children of the Light” or “Friends of the Truth,” but became widely known by a derisive name after he reportedly told a judge to “tremble at the Word of the Lord.” This pacifist movement played a critical role in the abolition of slavery in the British Empire. Which movement?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T16:26:25Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "quaker?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T16:26:26Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Wuacker", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T16:26:27Z", "username": "Nikhil Borra", "text": "Quakers", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T16:26:30Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Quakers", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T16:26:49Z", "username": "Kart